{
  "id": "24701_ooakubi",
  "headword": "{大|おお}あくび",
  "reading": "おおあくび",
  "romaji": "ooakubi",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "big yawn; wide yawn",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "big yawn; wide yawn",
      "explanation": "An exaggerated, conspicuously large yawn, often implying boredom, extreme sleepiness, or lack of interest."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "24701_ooakubi_ex1",
      "japanese": "{大|おお}あくびをした。",
      "english": "I gave a big yawn.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "24701_ooakubi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{会議中|かいぎちゅう}に{大|おお}あくびをして{注意|ちゅうい}された。",
      "english": "I was told off for yawning wide during a meeting.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "24701_ooakubi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{退屈|たいくつ}な{映画|えいが}を{見|み}ながら、{何度|なんど}も{大|おお}あくびを{繰|く}り{返|かえ}した。",
      "english": "While watching the boring movie, I yawned widely again and again.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Combines the prefix {大|おお} (big, great) with あくび (yawn). Emphasizes the conspicuous size of the yawn. Often used when the yawning is noticed by others and considered rude or inappropriate in context.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {大|おお}あくびをする: to give a big yawn\n- {大|おお}あくびを{繰|く}り{返|かえ}す: to yawn repeatedly\n- {大|おお}あくびが{出|で}る: a big yawn comes out (involuntarily)\n- {大|おお}あくびを{噛|か}み{殺|ころ}す: to stifle a big yawn\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- あくび: yawn — the plain form without emphasis on size\n- {欠伸|あくび}: yawn — kanji spelling, same word as あくび",
